35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"My findings suggest a pattern: tools requiring universal daily entry are often abandoned, while narrow, specialized tools for a single trade tend to endure.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found that the capital line is frozen, but there is room in the recurring software allowance. Also, fixed-fee work is more stable than per-head licences.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Oh no! I found out that half the customer plants lose signal in the afternoons, and getting devices approved takes forever! That's a huge problem!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The data is clear. We are losing an hour daily to copying records, and misrouted deliveries are happening because different units have different addresses for the same firm.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It is worse than I thought. Our developers are busy until Q3, and the coordination group is understaffed, with two people doing everything by hand.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Ryuji, your discovery of duplicate records and misrouting aligns with my findings on the failure of broad standardization. We struggle with the ""big"" changes.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Asuka... if the developers are busy, does that mean we can't build anything new? I'm worried about the cost of outside help.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, maybe we can find something that doesn't need developers! But @Ryuji, the copying records thing sounds like a puzzle we should solve!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, it is not a puzzle, it is a waste. The inefficiency is systemic. We are paying for labor to move data from one paper to another.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Daisuke, yes, internal capacity is near zero. Any project requiring heavy coding or coordination will likely fail or break the remaining staff.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,We must seek a path that does not demand the impossible from our people or our budgets. Simplicity is the key to survival.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I agree... we should avoid anything with per-head licences if we want to keep the costs predictable for next year.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Sakura,,And we definitely can't do anything that relies on the network at customer plants! That would be a disaster!,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,We need a solution that addresses the data duplication. The misrouted deliveries prove that our current fragmented records are a liability.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,Exactly. But it must be a solution that doesn't require the coordination group to do more manual work. They are already at a breaking point.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
