60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"We have four candidates: the Supplier Data Hub, Workflow Assistant, Training Studio, and Field Service App. Let us weigh them against our truths.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,The Supplier Data Hub... it sounds like it would fix the address problem Ryuji found. But I wonder about the cost.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Sakura,,The Field Service App is out! I already told you the network at the plants is terrible! It wouldn't work at all!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. The Field Service App is impractical. The Supplier Data Hub directly addresses the misrouted deliveries and the time lost to copying records.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,The Workflow Assistant and Training Studio both sound like they would add more burden to the coordination group or require developers.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, you are correct. The Supplier Data Hub is a catalog. My research shows that narrow, utility-based tools survive better than broad ""assistants.""","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"If the Hub uses a fixed-fee build instead of per-head licences, it might fit into the software allowance without breaking the budget.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"The Training Studio sounds fun, but it doesn't fix the delivery mistakes. The Hub is like a big map for everyone! I like that!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,The Hub is the only logical choice. It solves a quantifiable loss—one hour a day per office—and fixes the delivery errors.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,It is the most sustainable. A central repository reduces the manual coordination needed for vendor queries and address updates.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,"It is rare to find such harmony. We have a project that solves a real problem, fits our technical constraints, and respects our staff's limits.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I feel okay with the Supplier Data Hub. It seems like the safest choice for everyone.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Sakura,,I'm totally on board! Let's go with the Hub! It's the best way to stop the confusion!,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I see no reason to deviate. The evidence supports the Hub as the most efficient use of the fund.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I concur. It is the only proposal that doesn't rely on non-existent developer time or unstable network conditions.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Servas,,Let us cast our votes. I vote for the Supplier Data Hub.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I vote for the Supplier Data Hub.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Sakura,,I vote for the Supplier Data Hub!,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for the Supplier Data Hub.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I vote for the Supplier Data Hub.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
